   "explain": {
    "en": {
     "text": "A cube root undoes cubing. ∛27 = 3 because 3 × 3 × 3 = 27. Every rational number has exactly one cube root, and the cube root of a negative number is negative: ∛(−343) = −7. In exponent form ∛a = a^(1/3)."
    },
    "am": {
